{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgOdPPZK8ZyWOG8vmqt2B","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a set of independent shell and foundation components — Status Bar and Home Indicator, primary and secondary buttons, a tab bar with states, header variants, list rows, keypad key and pin dot, case row and account option, and a dialog — all composable in one build since none depend on each other, followed by the screens. I load Inter (Regular, Medium, Semi Bold, Bold, Extra Bold) and fix the system: light canvas #F6F5F3, white cards, ink #14141A, secondary #6E6E78, brand #FA5555, gain #0E9F6E, loss #E5484D, dark card gradient #1C1C22 to #2A2A33. I place the components library below the screens (y=1100+), lay out 414x896 screens at 474 spacing (01_Home x=0 through 07_Confirm x=2844), and recolor icon instances by walking descendants and setting vector fills.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":26240,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":43273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":26240}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bed43efa-734c-44d5-bcc6-cf27333fe398","uuid":"b6836312-301f-4f31-afa0-87fe5a6992e9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T08:42:54.209Z","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":12805}
